[00:08.88] How carefully I've shaped you in the solitude of days
[00:13.30] How peaceful is my mind entwined in cord around my fingers
[00:18.86] How sweet the days I've marked in knots I've tenderly caressed
[00:24.12] So many times I've touched you, reached you, teased you
[00:29.20] Now fingering these veins of hemp
[00:32.32] Their hair upon my skin
[00:35.48] And how gently, quickly you will sleep
[00:39.24] Slip into my collection with its bristles, coils, intentions
[00:45.08] Yet your words will be unfaithful before I set you free
[00:50.50] Slip as life is bound to slip from this entropy disorder
[00:55.30] Then tied and laid upon the floor in perfect symmetry
[01:00.06] 'Til the frayed edge of your lips on mine
[01:04.86] Positioned, placed at ease once more
[01:09.60] 'Til this restlessness returns I turn and turn and turn again
